{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE REDESIGN PAGE SHELL
  REFERENCE §6.7 · app-ux-standards §0.4
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The root is 100dvh and does not scroll. Exactly one element inside it does —
  `<main class="ag-main">` — so app bars, tab bars, action bars and the Gee
  launcher stay pinned without `position:fixed` and without the iOS address-bar
  jitter that comes with it.

  ── WHY THIS IS A LAYOUT AND NOT A BLOCK INSIDE gates.twig ───────────────────

  The first cut of the Phase 1 style page extended `layout/gates.twig` and put
  `.ag-shell` inside its `{% block content %}`. That renders, and it is wrong in
  a way that is obvious the moment you look at it: `.ag-shell` is `height:100dvh`
  with `overflow:hidden`, and the old layout's body scrolls, so the shell became a
  one-viewport-tall window onto a document that carried on underneath it. The page
  clipped at 844px, the legacy tab bar sat over the specimens, and the intro
  loader's globe painted across the whole thing.

  A shell that only works when nothing else owns the scroll cannot be a guest
  inside a layout that does. So it is its own layout, loading only the three
  redesign stylesheets, and pages converted by later phases extend THIS.

  `layout/gates.twig` keeps serving every unconverted page until Phase 9 retires
  it. Two layouts during a redesign is the honest state; one layout trying to be
  both is what produced the screenshot above.

  ── BLOCKS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    head_styles   page-local <style>, nonce'd
    header        SiteHeader — tablet and desktop      (Phase 2)
    app_bar       the phone AppBar, root or child      (Phase 2)
    content       goes inside <main>; the ONLY scroller
    bottom_bar    action bar OR tab bar, each [data-bottom-ui]  (Phase 2)
    foot_scripts  page-local <script>, nonce'd
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ lang|default('en') }}" dir="{{ (lang|default('en')) == 'ar' ? 'rtl' : 'ltr' }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  {# `viewport-fit=cover` so `env(safe-area-inset-*)` reports real numbers; without
     it every safe-area calculation in the components resolves to zero. #}
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>{{ page_title|default('Africa GATES') }}</title>
  {% if meta_description is defined %}<meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description }}">{% endif %}
  {% if meta_robots is defined %}<meta name="robots" content="{{ meta_robots }}">{% endif %}

  {# ── Display & reading, before first paint ────────────────────────────────
     Phase 2 owns the store and the settings screen. The hook is here because it
     has to run before any stylesheet paints — a linked file would paint first and
     the person who asked for 150% text would watch it start at 100%. #}
  {% block a11y_head %}{% endblock %}

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:wght@700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;700&display=swap">

  {# The three sheets, in cascade order. tokens.css is the single source of every
     colour, size, radius, shadow and duration; nothing else may carry a hex. #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/tokens.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/shell.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components.css') }}">
  {% block head_styles %}{% endblock %}
</head>

{# `ag-shelled` is what arms the overflow lock in shell.css. It is a class rather
   than a bare `html,body{overflow:hidden}` so the ~180 pages still on the old
   layout keep their document scroll — see the note at the top of shell.css. #}
<body class="ag-shelled" data-page="{{ page_id|default('') }}">
  <a class="ag-skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <div class="ag-shell">
    {% block header %}{% endblock %}
    {% block app_bar %}{% endblock %}

    <main class="ag-main" id="main">
      {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </main>

    {% block bottom_bar %}{% endblock %}
  </div>

  {% block gee %}{% endblock %}

  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/shell.js') }}"></script>
  {% block foot_scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
